# What never reaches the image build.
#
# .cargo/ is the load-bearing one and the least obvious. .cargo/config.toml is checked in and pins an
# ABSOLUTE target-dir of /home/agents/repo/lbsim/target, so several agents' checkouts share one build
# directory and cargo's own file lock serialises them. Inside a container that path is meaningless:
# cargo writes the binary there instead of ./target, and the next line of the Dockerfile fails with
# "./target/release/sim-run: not found" — exit 127, from a Cargo setting, with nothing in the error
# naming Cargo. Keep this exclusion whatever else changes.
.cargo/

target/
out/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
.git/
tests/
bench/
!bench/bode.py

# docs/ is excluded wholesale and then findings.md is put back, because the image serves that one file
# at /docs/findings.md. Order matters: the negation has to come after the exclusion.
docs/
!docs/findings.md
